*** Settings ***
Documentation       Business actions with customer data in the database - these keywords are used in tests.
Resource            ${EXECDIR}/resources/interactions/database_interactions.resource


*** Keywords ***
Start Example Database
    [Documentation]    Connects to the example database and creates the table "customer".
    Connect To Example Database
    Run Sql    CREATE TABLE customer (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT, city TEXT)
{%- if database_driver != 'sqlite' %}

Use Own Database
    [Documentation]    Connects to your own database.
    Connect To Own Database
{%- endif %}

Close Database
    [Documentation]    Closes the connection to the database.
    Disconnect Database

Create Customer
    [Documentation]    Creates a customer with name and city.
    [Arguments]    ${name}    ${city}
    Run Sql    INSERT INTO customer (name, city) VALUES ('${name}', '${city}')

Change City
    [Documentation]    Changes the city of a customer.
    [Arguments]    ${name}    ${new_city}
    Run Sql    UPDATE customer SET city = '${new_city}' WHERE name = '${name}'

Delete Customer
    [Documentation]    Deletes a customer.
    [Arguments]    ${name}
    Run Sql    DELETE FROM customer WHERE name = '${name}'
